<h2>What it does</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Log your period and flow, spotting, symptoms and how strong they are, energy, temperature, ovulation (LH) tests, cervical mucus and cervical position in a few taps.</li>
  <li>See your next period and your ovulation as ranges, with a plain-language confidence grade, never as a single promised day. Symptoms never move an estimate.</li>
  <li>A cycle dial shows where you are in your cycle; the calendar shows logged days, estimated days and the day of your cycle.</li>
  <li>Insights: cycle and period length, how they vary, how each estimate was worked out, and notes on food and movement for each phase with an evidence grade and sources.</li>
  <li>A report for your doctor, made on your phone as a PDF.</li>
  <li>Import your history from Natural Cycles, drip or a CSV file, and export everything whenever you like.</li>
  <li>Optional two-way sync with Apple Health and Health Connect, one data type at a time.</li>
  <li>Optional encrypted backup to your own iCloud Drive on iPhone. The file is encrypted on your phone before it leaves.</li>
  <li>App lock, discreet reminders, a discreet app icon and name, and screen protection.</li>
  <li>No analytics, no advertising, no tracking. Free, with nothing locked away.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Get Sanguine</h2>
<p>Coming soon to the App Store and Google Play, in Australia first.</p>

<h2>Open source</h2>
<p>Sanguine is free software under the AGPL. Read the code, check the claims above against it, or build it yourself: <a href="https://github.com/Amnesthesia/sanguine">github.com/Amnesthesia/sanguine</a>.</p>

<p class="note">Sanguine does not diagnose, screen for or treat any condition. If you are worried about your health, talk to a health professional.</p>
